    "About angle smoothing" : {

    },
    "About the angle line" : {

    },
    "After a run, the angle is lightly smoothed to remove sensor vibration jitter. The smoothing looks at each point's neighbours on both sides, so it doesn't shift the line in time — peaks stay where they happened. It only cleans up fast wiggle; it does not correct slow drift, and it never changes your stored measurements or your max angle. Very short runs can't be smoothed, so the raw angle is shown instead." : {

    },
